The function then uses two nested loops to compare each pair of adjacent elements in the array. If the current element is greater than the next element, they are swapped. This process continues until the end of the array, after which the outer loop iterates again, but this time the last sorted element will not be considered in the inner loop, reducing the number of comparisons needed.

The time complexity of this implementation is O(n^2) because in the worst-case scenario, the function will perform n * (n - 1) / 2 comparisons and swaps.

